 [camera notch](camera-notch.md).
+
+## Managed SSH capability 1
+
+A private embedding-manager capability enrolls new UUID roots without changing the public run protocol. The helper validates private `.omarchy-managed-ssh.json` metadata, the matching per-launch provisioning manifest and the exact stored TCP mapping to guest port 22. It sets the internal provisioning-share environment itself; a caller-supplied value is removed. The launch script attaches only that share, read-only, and signals opt-in through `tryomarchy.managed_ssh=1`.
+
+The embedding manager creates an independent client identity and guest host identity per VM. Only the guest host key and authorized public keys are shared. The guest timer waits for normal non-root owner provisioning, preserves the bound owner and host key across boots, and configures the vendor SSH service through a runtime drop-in. Password, interactive and root login are disabled for this opt-in mode. The ordinary authorized-keys file remains supported and untouched.
+
+Guest status carries the VM UUID, launch nonce, provisioning state and owner in an optional schema-1 field. The host validates bounded reports but treats them as advisory. Authenticated SSH must confirm the expected owner and VM/session identity before the manager reports readiness. Initial trust comes from the per-VM provisioning channel, never an unverified network key scan. Changed host identities require explicit recovery.
